_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nFound in Godot v4.6.3.stable. This is the only version I use.\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8134) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13420H (12 threads) - 15.70 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nChanges to \"scale\" in gdscript are reset, when physics movement (linear_velocity, apply_central_impulse) is involved.\nTweens can modify \"scale\", but \"scale\" is reset when a tween ends.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nStart main scene in project. Watch the three duck sprites:\nDuck_1 moves back and forth for 4 seconds in each direction. Setting scale to (-1, 1) in gdscript are immediatly reset to (1, 1).\nDuck_2 behaves as exepected. Setting scale to (-1, 1) flips the entire RigidBody2D.\nDuck_3 moves back and forth for 4 seconds in each direction while doubling it's size over 2 seconds using a tween. scale is reset to (1, 1) when tween ends.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[scale-error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29150225/scale-error.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.